  "domain_notes": [
    "from_ascii accepts a borrowed byte slice and scans to its first NUL. Native null char* is defined to produce Standard_RangeError; Rust empty input produces the same error result, but no raw nullable pointer API is claimed.",
    "from_utf16 is used only for at-least-36-unit valid storage. Native null or short UTF-16 pointers are outside defined input behavior because the constructor reads 36 units unconditionally.",
    "Clone::clone is the exact Rust method available for producing an owned copy; Guid also derives Copy, so ordinary Rust value copying needs no explicit call.",
    "operator= maps to Guid::assign, whose body copies the same UUID fields; Rust assignment of Guid itself is also available because Guid is Copy.",
    "The native std::hash specialization returns hash_code directly; the Rust Hash trait implementation is not treated as an equivalent hash-value target."
  ]
